formalpara.para:
the manufacturer code of the attribute to be retrieved. If -1
        is used, the method behaves exactly like
        {@link ZCLCluster#getAttribute(int)}

section.para:
Retrieve the current size of the internal raw frame (that is the size of
 the byte[] that would be returned if calling the {@link #getBytes()}
 method.

formalpara.para:
{@code true} if the ZCL Header Frame Control Field "Disable
         Default Response Sub-field" is 1. Returns {@code false}
         otherwise.

section.para:
Although this method allows write even 1 byte of the passed {@code int}
value, it is suggested to use the {@link #writeByte(byte)} because this
latter could be implemented in a more efficient way.

Although this method allows write even 1 byte of the passed {@code long}
value, it is suggested to use the {@link #writeByte(byte)} because this
latter could be implemented in a more efficient way.

formalpara.para:
One of the error codes defined above. If the returned error code
         is {@link #UNKNOWN_ERROR} and the {@link #hasZigBeeErrorCode()}
         returns {@code true} then the {@link #getZigBeeErrorCode()}
         provides the actual ZigBee error code returned by the device.

the Link Quality Indicator estimated by {@link ZigBeeNode}
         returning this for communicating with {@link ZigBeeNode}
         identified by the {@link #getNeighbor()}.

A promise representing the completion of this asynchronous call.
         In case of success, the resolved value will be a {@link Map}
         containing the Service.PID as {@link String} key of the
         {@link ZigBeeNode} service and the value the {@link ZigBeeRoute}
         for that node. In case of failure a {@link ZDPException}
         exception with the correct status code must be used to fail the
         promise.

A promise representing the completion of this asynchronous call.
         In case of success, the promise is resolved with a {@code null}
         value, otherwise with the correct {@link ZDPException} exception.
